     pitch (1 or 2 units) and the sheet preset (160x120, or
     A4/A3/A2 at 8 dots per unit - now that pages can leave on a
     laser or a plotter, the screenful is not the natural page
     for every drawing), and its FFrraammee button stamps the TEMPLATE
     /usr/vellum/etc/frame.d - ordinary drawing lines fed through
     the parser onto the frame layer, with $FF  $DD  $SS
     substituted in text values (file name, date, ``Sheet n/m'',
     revision) - so a company title block is an edit to that
     file, not a rebuild.  The sheet edge shows as a dotted con-
     struction guide.

